{"type":"WebSearch","query":"California Proposition 39 election results November 3 2026","content":"**Unofficial results for California Proposition 39 in the November 3, 2026, general election are not yet available.** The California Secretary of State’s election results site currently shows 0 precincts reporting (0 of approximately 23,860) and 0 votes counted for all statewide ballot measures, including Proposition 39, as of the latest update before polls close. Results will begin appearing after 8:00 p.m. Pacific Time on election night, with vote-by-mail, provisional, and other ballots continuing to be counted afterward. Official certification is expected by December 11, 2026.[[1]](https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county)

Proposition 39 is an initiated constitutional amendment titled “Prohibits Citizens From Voting Unless They Present Government-Issued Identification.” It would require in-person voters to show government-issued ID and mail voters to write the last four digits of a designated government-issued ID number on their ballot envelope (with unmatched or missing numbers invalidating the ballot). It also mandates that elections officials use government data to verify voter citizenship, report verification rates annually by county, provide free voter ID cards on request, and have the State Auditor conduct odd-year compliance audits. A “yes” vote would enact these changes; a “no” vote would keep current rules (primarily signature verification). Fiscal estimates put implementation costs in the tens to low hundreds of millions of dollars annually.[[2]](https://voterguide.sos.ca.gov/quick-reference-guide/39.htm)

Live tracking is available on the official California Secretary of State site (electionresults.sos.ca.gov), CNN, and local outlets like KCRA. Check those sources after polls close for updates, as early returns can shift significantly during the canvass period.","citations":["https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county","https://voterguide.sos.ca.gov/quick-reference-guide/39.htm"],"allowed_domains":null}
